    <p>Trade in pearls, spices, and precious stones flourished through ports like Puhar and Kaveripattinam. Archaeological finds of Roman amphorae and coins attest to robust Indo‑Roman commerce, while inland agrarian prosperity was ensured by sophisticated irrigation works such as the Grand Anicut.</p>

